Extension API: the build popup's queue as it is being edited ("BLDQ").

STATUS: NOT APPLIED — written by work order 180 (C3), parked for Data
(doc/briefs/180-parked-for-data.md, item 1.5).

PROOF (work order 180, 27 September 2026): this file is one step of a
series of six (open fixes 35-40, applied in that order on top of
orionlayer-local 9ab84230 — each appends its block after the previous
one). In a scratch clone of the engine, never on orionlayer-local:
`patch -p1 --dry-run` then `patch -p1` applied it cleanly on the steps
before it, and the patched src/ext/ext_api.cpp compiled with the engine's
own flags from out/build/Linux/linux-debug/build.ninja (the ORION2RE_EXT
and debug defines, every include directory, the cmake_pch.hxx include,
-fsyntax-only) — with a control: the same file with `_colony_auto_building` misspelt `_colony_autobuilding` was
refused. A full build of the whole series ran in scratch, only to record
the wire format for OrionLayer's fixtures.

To apply, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch, after ext_colony_product_cost.patch (38):

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_build_popup_queue.patch

then rebuild. It comes back off with `patch -R -p1` and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    COLBLDG edits a copy of the queue, _current_item[7], and writes it
    into the colony's producing[] only on OK or `<` / `>`
    (Do_Exit_Screen_Cleanup_, colbldg.cpp:2003-2016), so the wire shows
    the queue from BEFORE the popup until it closes. With it the popup's
    own state: the selection box (_active_prod, Draw_Active_Prod_
    :1792-1851), the mode a click is read in (_field_mode: 1 pick a
    design, 2 repeat; :1577-1582) and the autobuild radio's value.

WIRE, after CPRD, only while screen 25 is up:

    "BLDQ"  7 x int16 _current_item, 4 x int16 _active_prod,
            uint8 _field_mode, int16 _colony_auto_building

WHAT IT COSTS US WITHOUT IT: the build popup stays the game's own picture
(the safety net) — a queue HD cannot see is a queue HD cannot edit.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index dbe4a11a..6282f17a 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -537,6 +537,32 @@ static void SerializeState(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf,
         Write32(buf, ok ? COLCALC::Colony_Producing_Product_Cost_(&MOX::_colony[h]) : -1);
         Write16(buf, ok ? COLONY::Calculate_Current_Production_Turn_Count_(h) : (int16_t)-1);
     }
+
+    // 10. The build popup's queue as it is being edited: "BLDQ", written
+    //     ONLY while SCREEN_QUEUE_POPUP is up, and LAST. OrionLayer, open
+    //     fix 39.
+    //
+    //     COLBLDG edits a copy, _current_item[7], and writes it into the
+    //     colony's producing[] only on OK or `<` / `>`
+    //     (Do_Exit_Screen_Cleanup_, colbldg.cpp:2003-2016); until then the
+    //     wire shows the queue from before the popup. With it: the
+    //     selection box (_active_prod, Draw_Active_Prod_ :1792-1851), the
+    //     mode a click is read in (_field_mode: 1 pick a design, 2 repeat,
+    //     :1577-1582) and the autobuild radio's value (_colony_auto_building).
+    if (current_screen == SCREEN_QUEUE_POPUP) {
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'B');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'L');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'D');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'Q');
+        for (int i = 0; i < 7; i++) {
+            Write16(buf, COLBLDG::_current_item[i]);
+        }
+        for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+            Write16(buf, COLBLDG::_active_prod[i]);
+        }
+        Write8(buf, COLBLDG::_field_mode);
+        Write16(buf, COLBLDG::_colony_auto_building);
+    }
